// dictionaryList: the built-in dictionaries the recognisers know, one
// protoDictionary frame each, from which the system's dictionary list is made
// at boot (src/recognition/Dictionaries.h). In each frame: dictID is the id
// scripts use (GetDictionary, recConfig.dictionaries); ROMDictID the
// dictionary's number among the ROM's own Airus dictionaries, or
// localDictSlot the slot of the locale bundle that holds it; linkedDictID a
// further dictionary looked up with it; dictType 0 a word list, 1 a reverse
// (spelling) list, 4 a lexical (format) dictionary; domainType the input
// mask (view flags) whose fields it serves, its bottom bit (4097) marking a
// word list the spelling checker is not to offer from; status 1 for one
// enabled by default. The user (31), Expand (35) and Auto Add (36) ones are
// RAM dictionaries the user fills (limit: the most words they take).

dictionaryList := [|Array|:
	{
		_proto: @protoDictionary,
		name: "User (forward)",
		dictID: kUserDictionary,
		dictType: 0,
		domainType: vCharsAllowed + vNameField,
		order: 0,
		status: 1,
		count: 0,
		limit: 1000,
		addDuplicates: true
	},
	{
		_proto: @protoDictionary,
		name: "DarkStar (forward)",
